														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4511039">
									

<p>Yeah, the discovery addendum is kind of a leftover from an earlier draft where I included this whole storyline about a Person of Interest, with the addendum setting that storyline up for later. I do think that removing the discovery addendum altogether wouldn't work for me, however. I do feel that including the addendum acts as a little bit of a breather for what happens next (i.e. the exploration log), and that excluding it altogether would be a little bit&#8230; abrupt. However, that's just my pretentious side speaking there.</p>
<p>As for the final interview stuff? I'm going to make it a little more emotionally impactful at some point, although I'm probably going to leave it be for the time being.</p>
<p>Either way, thank you very much for your insight, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/t-rutherford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4620432); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4620432&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1582302044" alt="T Rutherford" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4620432)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/t-rutherford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4620432); return false;">T Rutherford</a></span>!</p>
<p><span style="font-size:50%;">If you couldn't tell, I have a crippling addiction to the <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[*user]]</span> function. Please send help</span></p>

